---
description: Use the SysML/KerML spec MCP instead of quoting the specification from memory
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user asks about SysML v2 or KerML language rules (names, namespaces, connectors, features, usages, constraints, grammar), call the `sysml-spec` MCP tools in this order:

1. `spec_element` if the question is about a named metaclass (Connector, Namespace, Feature, …)
2. `spec_route` to get clause ids without dumping text
3. `spec_search` for a short excerpt set (k ≤ 3)
4. `spec_get` only for the one clause that actually answers the question

Never paste large specification extracts into the chat. Cite clause numbers, say whether the passage is informative (typically clause 7) or normative (clause 8+), and include the highlighted viewer links returned by the tools.
